   "triage_title": "C8 nonauthor review of Math- frontiers/nongaussian_smoothing_admission_20261017/PROOF.md, slice H0 (p=0), with sympy controls and d=1 Monte Carlo (recovery/session_015wNj8LPTKXsaT68G3DgPPh/ng_review_20261019)",
   "triage_summary": "Provider-distinct review of the NG smoothing-admission theorem for p=0, d>=1, giving PASS_SCOPED with no must-fix. Sympy controls confirm the Jacobian 12 r^-(d+3), block identity (17), the constants 144*12^(-7/3)=12^(-1/3) and the cumulants 9504 and 8. A d=1 circle Monte Carlo of F=G+eps(H^2-1) finds the short-bar rate follows formula (6) (5.3201, 4.5991, 3.8689, 3.3923 for eps=0..3), not the covariance-matched Gaussian (4.1250, 2.8960, 2.2625), after grid-loss correction.",
